- AF-SCC-C2-VAC-GEN: SRC-025 (2001.11156, DOI 10.1007/s00220-020-03923-w), SRC-033 (DOI 10.1088/1361-6382/aadbcf)
- AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN: SRC-005 (1507.00601, DOI 10.4310/jdg/1518490820), SRC-021 (DOI 10.1002/cpa.20071)
- AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH: SRC-013 (DOI 10.2307/2118619), SRC-075 (1710.02922, DOI 10.1007/s00220-018-3157-1)

That's 8 rows: 2 per class, mix of arXiv/DOI.

Method: For each row:
- Locator used: prefer `https://api.crossref.org/works/{doi}` when DOI present (independent of the ledger's own `exact_locator`), else `https://export.arxiv.org/api/query?id_list={arxiv_id}`. Actually for arXiv rows the ledger used arxiv abs page. To be independent, use the arXiv API (export.arxiv.org) which returns Atom XML with title/authors/abstract — good.
- Fetch → record HTTP status, bytes, sha256 of raw response.
- Extract metadata: Crossref JSON gives title, author list, issued year, container-title, DOI; arXiv API gives title, authors, published year, abstract, journal_ref.
- Compare title (normalized: lowercase, collapse whitespace, strip punctuation), authors (last names count/subset), year, venue/container loosely; evidence_excerpt verbatim/normalized containment in fetched abstract.
- Verdicts: MATCH (metadata + excerpt match), MATCH-METADATA (metadata match, excerpt not available or partial), MISMATCH (contradiction), UNRESOLVED (fetch failed / not determinable).

Negative control: take one row where the excerpt matched, mutate the ledger excerpt (e.g., replace "vacuum Einstein equations" with "Einstein-Maxwell equations" or prepend a false claim), run the same comparator function → must return MISMATCH. Also a positive control: re-run on unmutated row → MATCH.

Important: the script should pin the input file sha256 and abort on mismatch (so the report is bound to frozen revision). Also record the exact ledger row content hash per citation.

Careful with network reliability in the sandbox: urllib with timeout, retries, User-Agent header (Crossref asks for mailto). Use proper UA "worker-072-spotcheck/1.0 (mailto:...)". Arxiv API rate limit: 1 request per 3 seconds; I'll sleep 3s between calls. Crossref: be polite.

I should save raw responses (or trimmed) into the artifact dir to make claims verifiable offline: e.g., `raw/SRC-002.crossref.json` and `raw/SRC-002.arxiv.xml` (or .txt). That makes the artifact self-contained and hash-verifiable. 8 rows * 2 sources is fine. Trim nothing; JSON responses can be large (Crossref full record ~50-100KB each; 8 = <1MB). arXiv XML ~10KB each. Acceptable. Actually to keep it bounded, save the full raw response but strip nothing — verifiability beats size.

